## Acceptance checks

- A deterministic red-capable real-host/minimized loop reproduces the observed initialization failure before the fix and passes afterward.
- The coder result records exact versions, checkout paths, runtime/process timeline, sanitized diagnostics, ranked hypotheses, proved cause, and why prior checks missed it.
- A red-before-green regression exercises the causal runtime/startup pattern, not only a mocked invocation.
- Host diagnostics causally distinguish synchronous spawn failure, early child execution failure, timeout, and a genuinely occupied peer; output is bounded and excludes media/artwork/environment data.
- Exact checkout-loaded OpenCode and Pi each initialize independently without the prior host error.
- Secure runtime and lifecycle behavior remain intact: owner-only artifacts, same UID, marker lease, singleton bind, incompatible/occupied peer preservation, detached daemon ownership, bounded retries, client disposal, and idle cleanup.
- Only repository-pinned Effect v4 APIs are used.
- All focused tests, package checks, and smokes below pass; no debug tag, generated package/runtime debris, or production daemon remains.
- The non-Apnea diff is narrow and evidence-backed. No verified history, docs, unrelated changes, or existing Apnea records are rewritten.

